, "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Idaho ranks among the most reliably Republican states in presidential politics, backing the Republican ticket by wide margins in every recent cycle. A partisan lean of roughly eighteen points Republican anchors the outlook, and the absence of an incumbent on the ballot does little to change the state's fundamental orientation. No general-election polling or expert ratings exist yet, so expectations rest on the state's durable partisan character.\n\nNational headlines point to headwinds for Republicans, with the sitting president's approval underwater across most states, but Idaho has resisted Democratic gains even in difficult Republican years. The open field could produce a contested Republican primary, yet the general election is expected to remain firmly in Republican hands. A Democratic win would require a shift far beyond anything seen in modern Idaho politics.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0246, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0539, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0537, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0553, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0476, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0546, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0466, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0509, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.049, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0539, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0538, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0585, "margin": -17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0558, "margin": -17.5}]}